#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:293
msgid "While active, users without the \"Bypass Deployment Guard\" capability cannot create, edit, delete, or restore content of a protected type; cannot manage protected taxonomies, menus, widgets, or Customizer settings; and cannot use the Site Editor. Scheduled posts of a protected type do not publish while the freeze is active — they remain scheduled and publish normally once it ends."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:294
msgid "Content changes made through the REST API, XML-RPC, WP-CLI, and WP-Cron events are blocked the same way. WP-Cron itself keeps running, and scheduled posts are held rather than lost. Changes that go around WordPress's own content functions and capability checks, such as direct database queries, cannot be blocked."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/SettingsPage.php:295
msgid "The public, logged-out frontend is never affected. Comments, users, plugins, themes, and general site settings are never affected. Users with the bypass capability, and Super Admins on Multisite, can always continue — but their changes can still be overwritten if a deployment or migration proceeds."
msgstr ""

